<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    THE ROLLBACK FLOOR (nexus-a0m60).

    A single tagDatabase changeset, included FIRST in db.changelog-master.xml,
    marking the bottom of the migration-owned schema. SchemaRollbackRoundTripIntegrationTest
    rolls back TO this tag; an operator performing a real rollback can aim at it
    by name.

    WHY A TAG AND NOT A COUNT. rollbackCount(N) is wrong in three separate ways
    here. N has to be re-derived every time a changeset lands. It silently covers
    the wrong set the first time a changeset is INSERTED rather than appended.
    And it counts DATABASECHANGELOG ROWS, so any cluster carrying the nexus-ixsxa
    duplicate rows (one per boot where a MARK_RAN runAlways precondition is unmet)
    reaches a different depth than the operator intended, drifting further with
    every boot. A tag is immune to all three and needs no maintenance.

    WHY FIRST IN MASTER, rather than just above the extension baseline. The
    extensions are created by vectors-001-1, which sits in the MIDDLE of master
    order — role-001, memory-001, plans-001, telemetry-*, t1-001, taxonomy-001,
    aspects-*, chash-001 and catalog-001 all precede it. So there is NO position
    that is simultaneously above the extensions and below every migration-owned
    table; a floor placed at the extensions leaves 26 tables beneath it,
    unreachable and untested (measured, 2026-07-27). The floor therefore goes at
    the very bottom, and vectors-001-1's extension rollback is declared
    irreversible instead — see the note there.

    SAFE TO INTRODUCE AFTER THE FACT. An ordinary changeset: it applies once on
    fresh databases and simply appends on already-migrated clusters. It creates
    no object, so there is nothing to conflict with and nothing to revert.

    NO <comment> CHILD, deliberately. The XSD makes tagDatabase and the normal
    changeSetChildren group (which <comment> belongs to) an EXCLUSIVE choice, so
    adding a comment makes the tagDatabase itself invalid with "Invalid content
    was found starting with element tagDatabase". Hence this prose lives here.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="floor-1-rollback-floor" author="nexus-a0m60">
        <tagDatabase tag="rollback-floor"/>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
